  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="8f7cc46d-a1c4-4f5a-a354-15049b2a8deb"><problem><para>
      <para>Here are a few pairs of positive numbers whose sum is 50.
        </para>
      <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>First number</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Second number</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Product</emphasis></entry></row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>a</entry>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>49</entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>b</entry>
            <entry>2</entry>
            <entry>48</entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>c</entry>
            <entry>10</entry>
            <entry>40</entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para> Find the product in Row a.
          </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </para></problem><solution><para>49</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 49.
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
